# Royal Z Lanes — Cursor Rules

You are working on a bowling alley lane reservation system built with Next.js 16, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, Prisma, and Stripe Connect.

## Before writing any code

1. Read .claude/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md — all visual decisions come from the token system
2. Read .claude/STACK_BASELINE.md — frozen stack decisions, Next.js 16 API notes
3. Check docs/wireframes/ for the screen you are building
4. Read .claude/BOOKING_DOMAIN.md — business logic and data model
5. Read the relevant .claude/contracts/*.md for the surface you are touching

## Non-negotiable rules

**Colors**: ONLY CSS custom properties. Never raw hex. Never Tailwind color classes.
```
RIGHT: color: var(--color-text-secondary)
WRONG: color: var(--palette-stone-500)   ← palette tokens are for tokens.css only
WRONG: color: '#57534E'
WRONG: className="text-stone-500"
```

**Components**: 4-layer system — tokens → ui/ primitives → patterns/ → pages
- Pages: layout and composition only. No colors, no borders, no typography.
- Patterns in components/patterns/: compose from ui/ only.
- Primitives in components/ui/: only place each element is styled.

**Tailwind**: OK for layout/spacing. Never for color or dark mode.
Never use `dark:` prefix — data-theme attribute handles both modes.

**Fonts**: var(--font-display) for Fraunces, var(--font-body) for DM Sans. Never hardcode.

**Lane count**: getLaneCount(bowlerCount) from src/lib/lane-logic.ts — always.
Never inline Math.ceil(bowlerCount / 6) in a component or page.

**Max online booking**: 18 bowlers. Groups larger than 18 → prompt to call.

**Tenant**: Never hardcode venue name, address, phone, or colors.
Always read from getTenant(). Drift sentinel greps for literal venue strings.

**Refunds**: Server-side only. MANAGER or ADMIN role required. STAFF cannot refund.
Walk-in/phone bookings have no Stripe payment — use manualRefundBookingAction.

**Staff app**: data-theme="dark" in layout. Customer app: data-theme="light".
Both use the same --color-* and --surface-* token namespace.
The theme system handles light/dark — never add separate --staff-* tokens.

**Money**: All monetary values are integer cents. Never Decimal, never float.
calculatePrice() returns integer cents. formatPrice() divides by 100 at display.

**Stripe**: Never import stripe directly. Only through src/lib/stripe.ts.
**Email**: Never import resend directly. Only through src/lib/email.ts.
**Auth**: Never import next-auth directly. Only through src/lib/auth.ts.

**Schema changes**: Read .claude/SCHEMA_MIGRATIONS.md before touching schema.prisma.
Never add columns from Part 2 of BOOKING_DOMAIN.md without confirming the
migration has been planned, reviewed, and run.

## .claude/ file hierarchy (source of truth order)

When files conflict, later entries override earlier:
1. STACK_BASELINE.md — framework and infrastructure decisions
2. BOOKING_DOMAIN.md — business logic and data model
3. SCHEMA_MIGRATIONS.md — planned schema changes (gates Part 2 of BOOKING_DOMAIN)
4. DESIGN_SYSTEM.md — visual system
5. contracts/*.md — surface-specific contracts
6. STAFF_INTERACTIONS.md — staff/admin global rules and architecture
7. staff/0N_*.md — staff surface-specific interaction specs
8. BOOKING_INTERACTIONS.md — customer booking behavior
9. CUSTOMER_DASHBOARD.md — customer post-booking experience

These .claude/ files override any other docs in the project.

## File locations
- Tokens:          src/styles/tokens.css
- Primitives:      src/components/ui/
- Patterns:        src/components/patterns/
- Chrome:          src/components/chrome/
- Business logic:  src/lib/
- Customer pages:  src/app/(customer)/
- Staff pages:     src/app/(staff)/
- Admin pages:     src/app/(admin)/
- Wireframes:      docs/wireframes/

## Current booking flow routes
- /book              — bowler count + date/time (Step 1)
- /book/package      — package selection (Step 2)
- /book/details      — shoe sizing per bowler (Step 3)
- /book/confirm      — review + payment (Step 4)
- /book/success      — confirmation page (Step 5)

## Staff/Admin architecture
- /staff             — staff cockpit (STAFF+ role)
- /admin             — admin settings (MANAGER+ role)
- Both share AppShell + NavRail chrome
- Two route groups for auth gating, one visual experience
- Never merge into a single route group
